            <ArticleTitle>[Experience of off-pump coronary artery bypass grafting with starfish heart positioner].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>385-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Recent advances in off-pump coronary artery bypass (OPCAB) technique have demonstrated that multivessel coronary revascularization can be safely performed in selected patient without cardiopulmonary bypass. Numerous positioning technique and devices have been developed to assist access to coronary vessels during OPCAB, such as deep pericardial suture, surgical pads, and cardiac positioning device and stabilizers. We used new cardiac positioning device Starfish heart positioner (Medtronic Corporation) for 2 case of OPCAB. Starfish heart positioner was very useful to successfully perform multivessel coronary bypass on all walls of the beating heart. Starfish heart positioner will facilitate and expand the ability to easily and consistently perform OPCAB.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
